<h1>Willie Wilson</h1>
<p>Businessman, fourth run for mayor. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>Founder of Omar Medical Supplies, former McDonald&#39;s franchisee, and producer of the gospel show Singsation; 78, a sharecropper&#39;s son from Louisiana who left school in the seventh grade. This is his fourth run for mayor, funded mostly with his own money.</p>
<p><a href="/directdemocracy/app/candidate/Mg0DTiPuSyRCjXnNjBWneSPfX5u1">Full platform, open to comments</a></p>
<p><a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (williewilson2027.com)</a></p>
<h2>What sets them apart</h2>
<p>Only Wilson: No CPS diploma without a trade certificate, and no promotion to the next grade without meeting state standards.</p>
<p>Pensions: Ask voters to change the state constitution so pension costs can be dealt with. Quigley and Cardenas would have workers share the cost.</p>
<p>Taxes: Cut taxes for working people and businesses. Kelly and Kitover promise no new ones; Johnson and Giannoulias want the wealthy to pay more.</p>
<p>Bears: Supports keeping the Bears in Chicago. No other platform mentions the team.</p>
<h2>Where they split from the field</h2>
<p>New taxes: Cut taxes. Make the wealthy pay more: Johnson and Giannoulias. No new taxes: Kelly and Kitover. Savings first, before any new revenue: Quigley.</p>
<p>Pensions: Change the state constitution. Workers share the cost: Quigley and Cardenas. Restructure the funds and pay ahead: Giannoulias and Mendoza. Bankruptcy on the table: Kitover.</p>
<h2>In their words</h2>
<ul>
<li>No CPS diploma without a trade certificate, and no promotion to the next grade without meeting state standards. <q>I will expand trade programs in schools and require students to be certified in a trade before they can graduate.</q> (<a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign platform (williewilson2027.com)</a>)</li>
<li>Ask voters to change the state constitution so the city can deal with its pension costs. <q>If we do not make some difficult decisions the pension debt will consume our budget.</q> (<a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign platform (williewilson2027.com)</a>)</li>
<li>Cut taxes for working people and businesses. <q>I will cut taxes for working class citizens and businesses.</q> (<a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign platform (williewilson2027.com)</a>)</li>
<li>Treats housing as a right, and supports keeping the Bears in Chicago. <q>I view housing as a right. Homeownership is the cornerstone of wealth building.</q> (<a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">williewilson2027.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Willie Wilson for Mayor 2027</li>
<li>Raised: $404K</li>
<li>Spent: $413K</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $48K</li>
<li>Since the committee formed May 19, 2026, through Sept. 30. $400,000 of the third quarter&#39;s money was loans from the candidate; the committee owes him $450,000. <a href="https://elections.il.gov/CampaignDisclosure/CommitteeDetail.aspx?id=41192" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>6% of likely voters in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 15 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Would cut taxes for working people and businesses, bring in revenue through new businesses, and ask voters to change the state constitution so pension costs can be dealt with.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>I will cut taxes for working class citizens and businesses.</q> (<a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign platform (williewilson2027.com)</a>)</li>
<li><q>If we do not make some difficult decisions the pension debt will consume our budget.</q> (<a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign platform (williewilson2027.com)</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
<h2>Also on the record</h2>
<ul>
<li>Produces Singsation, the first nationally syndicated Black-owned gospel TV show, and has run for president and the US Senate under his own Willie Wilson Party. (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willie_Wilson_(businessman)" rel="nofollow noopener">en.wikipedia.org</a>)</li>
</ul>
